{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Silly Superstitions", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Breaking a Wishbone", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 17, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects  in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed to", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The structure <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span> is used to talk about expectations, obligations or arrangements.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">be supposed to</span>, in past, present or future.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "The structure is:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "subject + to be + supposed to + verb", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">You <span class=\"strong\">weren't supposed to </span>make the cranberry sauce. <br/>I <span class =\"strong\">was supposed to</span> cook the turkey. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "**Pronunciation tip**:<br/>When you say supposed to, you link the /d/ and /t/ sounds together. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Like this:<br/>Be suppose_to", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I wasn't supposed to cook the mashed potatoes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You were supposed to make a wish.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " I was supposed to play this year.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I wasn't supposed to participate.<br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Conditional Sentences with <span class=\"italic\">If</span> Clause", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "The <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span> with if clauses is used to exchange opinions about possible future outcomes. <br> The <span class=\"strong\">second conditional </span>  is used to exchange opinions about unreal or imaginary (hypothetical) situations in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " In conditionals, we have two clauses: the if clause and the condition clause. When the if clause is the first part of the sentence, write a comma before the condition clause. <br><br> To say that something is possible, use the <span class=\"strong\">first conditional </span>  (will or will not do something). In that condition, something else may, may not, will, or will not happen. <br><br>  <span class=\"prelo-letter-page-break\"></span>You use the <span class=\"strong\">second conditional</span> to talk about unreal or hypothetical situations. There is no certainty that it's possible to fulfill the condition.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\">If I had a million dollars, I would buy a car.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  Do you have a million dollars?  No.<br/> Is it possible to suddenly get a million dollars? Not really.<br/> What would you do if you had a million dollars? Buy a car.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional:\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"First Conditional: 2nd Clause\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If I finish work today, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I'll come to the dinner tonight.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It's possible that I can go to the dinner tonight, but only if finish working first. \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "If my mom could only choose one holiday to enjoy for the rest of her life, she would choose Thanksgiving.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "If I had one wish, I would wish it to be Thanksgiving everyday.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional:<br/>If ... + Simple Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Second Conditional: <br/>would + base verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> If I had one meal left to eat in my life, </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I would choose my mom's Thanksgiving dinner.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" It is an impossible situation and can only happen in a hypothetical situation.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "commercial", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to \u200bbuying and \u200bselling things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: For my mom, Halloween has become too commercial.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about Thanksgiving.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get together", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to gather or assemble", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My mom enjoys it when family and friends get together and share a big meal. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "mashed potatoes", "type": "name"}, {"content": " \u200bpotatoes that have been \u200bboiled and \u200bcrushed until they are \u200bsmooth", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Last year, I was supposed to cook mashed potatoes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "cranberry sauce", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sauce made from a \u200bsmall, round, \u200bred \u200bfruit with a \u200bsour \u200btaste", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was supposed to make the cranberry sauce.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "instead", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in \u200bplace of someone or something \u200belse", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Instead, my little cousin won.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to yank", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to \u200bpull something forcefully with a \u200bquick \u200bmovement", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rules are simple; each person grabs an end and gives a yank. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to disallow", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to say \u200bofficially that something cannot be \u200baccepted because it has not been done in the \u200bcorrect way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was supposed to play this year, but my mother disallowed it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "participant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who takes part in or becomes involved in a particular activity", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Participants are always selected by my mother. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le17ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"ty