ate_override": 1, "type": "video", "id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"type": "video", "value": {"video_src": "engenn8le17ob06re2vid02", "images": [{"image": "", "text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0"}, {"image": "", "text": "I love Halloween. It is my favorite time of the year, but it is not for everyone. Halloween was loved by my mom, but she has recently changed her opinion. For my mom, Halloween has become too commercial.", "id": 1, "time": "100"}, {"image": "", "text": "If my mom could choose only one holiday to enjoy for the rest of her life, she would choose Thanksgiving. My mom enjoys it when the family and friends get together and share a big meal. She loves to cook, which is good, because I don't. Last year, I was supposed to cook mashed potatoes and I was supposed to make the cranberry sauce, two dishes my family loves to eat. However, I made a mess of both dishes so badly that my mom had to recook them. Everything tasted amazing though, as always. If I had one meal left to eat in my life, I would choose my mom's Thanksgiving dinner.", "id": 2, "time": "13600"}, {"image": "", "text": "Now, Thanksgiving has its own superstition and that is the breaking of the wishbone. In my parent's house, the breaking of the wishbone is a family tradition. The rules are simple; each person grabs an end and gives a yank. If you get the bigger piece, your wish will be granted. Participants are always selected by my mother. I was supposed to play this year, but my mother disallowed it. I guess I've had enough good luck recently. Instead, my little cousin won. His wish: \u201cIf I had one wish, I would wish it to be Thanksgiving every day.\u201d\nA perfect wish.", "id": 3, "time": "50000"}]}}], "_data": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "type": "sena"}